Suppose I have a product with combinations. I want to set combinations' prices and unit prices based solely on combination's impact on both prices, so I set the price/unit price (both of them) to zero on the product and the price impact/unit price impact to the desired values. Of course, I set the unity to the desired value, too.
When I click on the "Save" button, it will change nothing - as long as either the product unit price or the combination price impact are zero, even if all that matters is their sum, PrestaShop will incorectly conclude the final unit price is zero.
And, since the unit price is passed as zero to the theme, the theme will show nothing.

There are the #34260 and #34418 issues about the error on saving zero unit prices. PR #34419 removed the artificial constraints enforced on the form prices, but there is still such a constraint in the Product class in the `computeUnitPriceRatio()` method (lines 5883-5885):
